== Asynchronous ETL
We implemented two asynchronous data sources, `AsyncSQLSource` and `AsyncMergeJoiningSource`, to test whether extraction can overlap with downstream ETL work. `AsyncSQLSource` extends `SQLSource` with asynchronous database connections and batched retrieval. A producer task fetches batches into a bounded `asyncio` queue while the consumer processes previously fetched rows. The configurable `prefetch` parameter limits buffered batches and therefore bounds memory use.

`AsyncMergeJoiningSource` adapts `pygrametl`'s merge-join approach to asynchronous iterators, which the synchronous `MergeJoiningSource` cannot consume directly. It asynchronously advances through two sources sorted by join key, matching rows without loading either complete dataset into memory. When keys repeat, it buffers matching rows from the second source to produce all corresponding combinations.
